Yeah, I've seen a problem like this but asking for  $xy.$ <details><summary>Solution</summary>After some experimentation, we see that dividing the equations gives us what we want, i.e. the left-hand side becomes
\begin{align*}
\frac{x+\tfrac{1}{y}}{y+\tfrac{1}{x}} &= \frac{x^2y+x}{y^2x+y} 
&= \frac{x(xy+1)}{y(xy+1)} 
&= \frac{x}{y}.
\end{align*}
Hence, the answer is   $$ \frac{20}{24}=\boxed{\frac{5}{6}}. $$    $\square$</details>

