Note that  $\angle CBD = \angle DBA = 60^{\circ}$ , so  $\overline{BD}$  bisects  $\angle CBA$ . Since  $\tfrac{AB}{BC}=\sqrt{\tfrac{225}{100}}=\tfrac{3}{2}$ ,  $\tfrac{AD}{DC}=\tfrac{3}{2}$  as well by the Angle Bisector Theorem. Note that  $\triangle BDC \sim \triangle EDA$ , so  $\tfrac{[\triangle BCD]}{[\triangle EDA]}=\left(\tfrac{3}{2}\right)^2=\tfrac{9}{4}$ . If the area of the shaded region is  $6x$ , then  $[\triangle BDC]=4x$  and  $[\triangle EDA]=9x$ . Then,  $6x+9x=225$ , so  $x=15$ , for a requested answer of  $6x=\boxed{\textbf{(B) }90}$ .</details>

